INT. CITY PLANETARIUM - DOME - NIGHT

Stars wheel overhead. Twenty invited guests, seated in recliners. INSPECTOR ILSE MORROW, 40s, stands at the rail by the projector.

ILSE
Nobody leaves. Nobody speaks.

The stars blink out. Total dark. A SCREAM. A thud.

Lights snap on. TANVEER KHATRI, 50s, the curator, lies sprawled below the projector, a brass key in his fist. Everyone freezes.

BEATA LOWENSTEIN, 30s, the donor, and COSIMO FERRANTE, 60s, the rival, point at each other.

BEATA / COSIMO
(together)
He did it!

BEATA
I never touched him!

COSIMO^
I was across the room!

WREN, 20s, the usher, bolts for the exit. DOYLE, 40s, the security guard, tackles her. Both crash into a row of recliners. The seats fold.

ILSE
Enough!

Tanveer sits up, groaning, rubbing his skull.

TANVEER
Who turned off my sky?

Everyone breathes out. Ilse pockets her badge, almost smiling.
